## 2026-08-15 — RESEED: MODULE-LOCAL rodata label namespaces (the prerequisite for a per-module emit cache).
# `.Lstr<N>` was a single literal counter threaded across modules IN PARSE ORDER, and `.Lfld`/`.Lflt` keyed on
# ABSOLUTE offsets into the concatenated source buffer. Measured consequence: adding ONE string literal to
# module 4 changed 13 of the 19 per-module GAS blocks — and almost every emit change in this compiler adds a
# `push_str(sb, "…")`. That made per-module invalidation track PARSE ORDER rather than the meaning of the edit,
# which would have halved the value of any incremental cache.
# Scheme: `MODTAB` holds two monotone non-decreasing bases per module (source-offset base, label-index base),
# module 0 pinned to 0; every label emits as `(m(k), k - base[m(k)])`. Label-index bases are recovered by
# REPLAYING the real .rodata walk in a silent scan mode, so no match arm can be missed.
#   .Lstr<N>   -> .Lstr<m>_<n>      .Lflt<off> -> .Lflt<m>_<n>      .Lfld<off> -> .Lfld<m>_<n>
# UNIQUENESS is unconditional, not empirical: for any non-decreasing base array with base[0] == 0 the map
# k -> (m(k), k - base[m(k)]) is INJECTIVE (recover k = base[m] + n), so this is a pure RENAMING of the old key
# — distinct labels stay distinct, equal stay equal. Every subtle property of the old scheme therefore survives:
# the HOF-clone (fnpos+1)*1000000 renumber, the .Lflt dedup, the `lbl % 1000000 >= 500000` embed marker, and
# cross-module references from inlined bodies and monomorphized instances. A wrong base can only cost cache
# precision, never correctness.
# Invalidation radius after (scripts/incr_probe.sh blast, 19 blocks): body edit 1, comment 0, layout edit 4
# (its users), ADDED STRING LITERAL 13 -> 1.
# seed(old) builds Stage1; Stage1 == Stage2 == Stage3 byte-identical GAS (776233 lines) AND byte-identical
# binaries (sha 138a142c…); full e2e green (1244 ok) + a64/rv64/wasm sweeps clean under Stage2.
# Landed together with the per-module .o split unblock (a 64-byte name StrBuf, NOT the codegen fault it was
# long believed to be) — `ALATYR_OSPLIT=1` builds green, 19 objects, .text/.rodata/.data byte-identical to the
# single-.s binary. REMAINING absolute-offset key: a lifted lambda's `<module>__lam<fnpos>` symbol.

